.TH BRATAN-TIDY 1 "2026" "BratanOS" "BratanOS Manual"
.SH NAME
bratan-tidy \- keep BratanOS clean
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bratan-tidy
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TASK ...]
.br
.B bratan-tidy
.B --status
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reclaims disk space and removes leftover trash from common Arch sources:
orphan packages, pacman cache, old kernel modules, .pacnew/.pacsave files,
orphan user-config directories, journald logs and broken symlinks.
.PP
Runs as a dry-run by default. Pass
.B --apply
to actually delete things.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --apply
Actually remove things.
.TP
.B --auto
Non-interactive mode used by systemd timers and pacman hooks.
.TP
.B --status
Print a summary of reclaimable space and exit.
.TP
.BI --keep-cache= N
Pacman cache versions to keep (default 2).
.TP
.BI --keep-kernels= N
Old kernel sets to keep (default 2).
.TP
.BI --journal-days= N
Vacuum journal entries older than N days (default 14).
.SH TASKS
orphans, cache, kernels, pacfiles, userconfigs, journal, symlinks.
.SH FILES
/etc/bratanos/tidy.conf
.br
/usr/lib/systemd/system/bratan-tidy.timer
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR paccache (8),
.BR pacdiff (8),
.BR journalctl (1).
